<?xml version='1.0' encoding='UTF-8'?>
<Project Type="Project" LVVersion="25008000">
	<Property Name="NI.Project.Description" Type="Str">This example shows how Safety Config is used for RobotDrive outputs.  By default Safety Config is enabled for RobotDrive.  This means that RobotDrive must be called at least every 100 ms.  Otherwise the motor outputs will be turned off until RobotDrive gets called.

1. Set up your robot and wiring.
2. Run this VI.
3. Increase the loop delay to 300 ms.  This simulates what happens if other code is starving the drive loop code.  When the loop delay is large enough, the Safety Config will turn off the RobotDrive motors.  You will likely see the motors pulse on and off, because when Safety Config is enabled RobotDrive needs to be called at least every 100 ms.
4. With the loop delay still at 300 ms, Select &lt;B&gt;Safety Config Off&lt;/B&gt;.  This disables Safety Config - you can disable as needed in your program.

This example uses radio buttons to enable and disable Safety Config.

This example expects a USB cable connected from your development PC to the Type B USB Jack (next to the power input) on the roboRIO.

This example requires the Driver Station to be running with Teleoperated Enabled.</Property>
